02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1210:### 25.7 Operational artifact governance
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1213:- distinguish packet presence from linked operational evidence
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1214:- preserve stable identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` across benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, and telemetry artifacts
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1215:- prefer `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Critique delta ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, and `Telemetry drift investigation memo` when the live control problem requires linked execution evidence rather than a summary verdict
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1216:- do not let `Benchmark execution report`, `Replay suite verdict memo`, `Release evidence bundle v2`, or `Telemetry trend memo` imply a stronger controller or runner substrate than the evidence actually supports
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1217:- if operational artifacts are absent, if only partial completion is visible, or if unresolved join failure blocks one gate, downgrade gate confidence before release, promotion, or drift escalation
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1219:- let a newer compatible artifact supersede its stale predecessor explicitly rather than keeping both live by habit
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1220:- before joining operational artifacts, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness; reject incompatible merges that would weaken a stronger artifact
02_overlays/PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay.md:1221:- preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in any joined artifact that survives release or telemetry review
